.TH MORE 1 2026-09-25 "Substrate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
more \- page through text one screenful at a time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B more
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B more
is a minimal pager.
It copies
.I file
(or standard input if no
.I file
is given) to standard output, pausing after every 23 lines.
It has no options, does not query the terminal size, and supports no
commands other than those described here.
Only the first
.I file
operand is used; any others are ignored.
.PP
At each pause
.B more
prints
.B \-\-More\-\-
and reads one character from standard input.
If the character is
.BR q ,
.B more
exits.
Any other character erases the prompt and shows the next 23 lines.
Because the terminal is normally in canonical mode, the response
takes effect only after
.B Enter
is pressed, and the newline itself is read as the response to the
following pause.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including quitting with
.BR q .
.TP
.B 1
.I file
could not be opened.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cat (1),
.BR head (1),
.BR pr (1),
.BR tail (1)
.SH BUGS
Responses to the prompt are read from standard input, which is also
where the text comes from when no
.I file
is given.
Paging a pipe therefore consumes input bytes as responses instead of
waiting for the keyboard.
.PP
Input is read one byte at a time.
